1️⃣ Transport Layer

Transport Layer is Layer 4 of the OSI model.

Its main responsibilities:

Process-to-process delivery

Segmentation

Reassembly

Flow control

Error control

Connection management

Multiplexing/demultiplexing


Application
     ↓
👉 Transport Layer
     ↓
Network
     ↓
Data Link

Main protocols:

TCP
UDP


---

2️⃣ TCP vs UDP — Most Important

TCP	UDP

Connection-oriented	Connectionless
Reliable	Unreliable/best-effort
Ordered delivery	No guarantee of ordering
Flow control	No TCP-style flow control
Congestion control	No TCP-style congestion control
ACKs	No TCP ACK mechanism
Retransmission	Yes
More overhead	Less overhead
Slower generally	Faster/lower overhead generally


Easy memory:

> TCP = Trustworthy



> UDP = Uncomplicated




