1️⃣5️⃣ SYN Consumes One Sequence Number

This is a classic GATE trap.

Suppose:

SYN:
Seq = 500

The SYN consumes one sequence number.

Therefore server responds:

ACK = 501

Similarly, FIN also consumes one sequence number.


---

🔥 1️⃣6️⃣ TCP Connection Termination

TCP normally uses a 4-step termination because each direction is closed independently.

Client                         Server

   FIN ──────────────────────→
        ←──────────────── ACK

        ←──────────────── FIN
   ACK ──────────────────────→

So:

> Connection establishment → 3-way handshake



> Connection termination → commonly 4 segments




---

1️⃣7️⃣ Why 4 Steps?

TCP is full duplex.

Each direction can be closed independently.

Client → Server
   CLOSE

Server → Client
   CLOSE

Hence the FIN/ACK exchange in each direction.


